Hello, Lark campers!

This is your email reminder to take your COVID test right away, since it is within 48 hours of your arrival to camp!

Please also review the [Lark Camp’s 2026 Covid policy](https://docs.google.com/document/d/17FNMuB0wKMtitEgTzT5jI00kjvadnEzKmLbX_toSm00/edit) to learn about how we’re handling **testing**, **refunds** (where applicable) and **communication** about any active cases that may arise at camp.

### Lark 2026 Covid Basics

* **Negative Covid test** - Each camper must show proof of a negative Covid test result at the entry gate upon arrival, from a test taken within the previous 48 hours. Photos or result printouts/screenshots are accepted **at the gate only**; please do not email them to us.
* **Testing at the entry gate will cost $15** for the test itself, and the camper may not enter camp until a negative result is seen.
* **Bring N95 Masks** - Lark recommends that everyone bring one or more well-fitted N95 masks for the week, in case there is a positive Covid case at camp. (Pleated masks stop liquids, but not viruses.)
* **Free N95s** - Thanks to a donation from MaskblocSunsetSF, Lark can offer one additional free N95 mask per camper in case of need. Adult and child sizes available. You can pick one up at any camp office.
* **Bring rapid tests** - We also recommend that everyone bring one or more rapid tests, in the case of a positive test at camp. Remember to check the expiration date, and then check online if that date has been extended by the FDA.
* **Additional rapid tests** - Lark has received a donation of 48 rapid tests to share for free. As of this writing, we are trying to secure at least 200, but haven’t yet. Note: this stock of tests is slated for use **after** entry; entry gate tests will cost $15.
* **Test yourself** - If you feel woozy or ill, get tested! It might be just the dust (and no sleep, and…) but it might not be. Protect your fellow campers' safety.
* **Positive cases** - **If you test positive, immediately let a camp staffer know,** and isolate yourself from other campers until you can safely leave camp. You will be given help and support, and a prorated refund.
* **Communications** - If a positive case occurs during camp, staff will make announcements, and will post current information on the doors of kitchens, halls, and shuttles.

**For more details, please see our [Covid policy document](https://docs.google.com/document/d/17FNMuB0wKMtitEgTzT5jI00kjvadnEzKmLbX_toSm00/edit)!**
